{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794791545,"nonce":"klDsIYaZu5qoxeXSHbonGtwfqsc=","message":"Correction to the previous comment: the explanation that the text input's own move handler causes the extra idle commits is wrong. The text input registers only enter/leave and drag handlers (widgets/text_input/handlers.rs), and drag is exempt from the redraw gate and only arrives with a button held. The blink (400 ms, text_input/runtime.rs) explains about 2.5 commits per second; the remaining ~3.5 per second with the pointer over the field are unexplained (other nodes with move handlers, pointer_query, hover-driven state_changed?). Measured only: pointer motion over the field raises idle commits to about 6 per second in a virtual KWin, motion over empty background does not. For fs-blinc-5 or later: log the reason for each invalidation first, and fix only what that log shows.","files":null}]}